==Battleground==
*2 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 22.67~24 seconds<sup>680f~720f</sup>.
*5 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 16~17.33 seconds<sup>480f~520f</sup>.
*1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Iguanidae Ibilujon]] spawns as the boss.
**6 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 49.33~50.67 seconds<sup>1,480f~1,520f</sup>.
**6 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 49.33~50.67 seconds<sup>1,480f~1,520f</sup>.
**10 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 49.33~50.67 seconds<sup>1,480f~1,520f</sup>.
**6 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 49.33~50.67 seconds<sup>1,480f~1,520f</sup>.
**2 [[Haniwanwan]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 69.33~70.67 seconds<sup>2,080f~2,120f</sup>.
**1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns after 180 seconds<sup>5,400f</sup>.
**1 [[Golem Sunfish]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Because of Iguanidae Ibilujon, it is highly advised to beat [[Atonement for Sin]] in order to unlock the True Forms of [[Uncanny Legends]]' Legend Cats. Without them, this stage becomes nigh-impossible thanks to the unbelievably powerful pushing power of every enemy here.

Your goal is to kill Iguanidae Ibilujon as quickly as possible, before you're overwhelmed by the Relic enemies. Its recommended to bring one [[Wave Shield]] such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to help with the occasional Haniwanwans, alongside [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]/[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to siphon some extra cash from Relic Doges and the aforementioned Haniwanwans. Golem Sunfish will ensure you can never stack too many units, so beware of wasting too much cash.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] - An excellent nuker in this stage, as his [[Long Distance]] ability can help you hit enemies behind peons and has decent survivability, allowing him to stay on the battleground and keep dealing high amounts of damage.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] - A great DPS option, as it has a guaranteed chance to [[Weaken]] everything in this stage except for Ibilujon, and can deal some phenomenal chip damage. Its second form is not recommended for use due to its lower health, lack of guaranteed Weaken and not having [[Behemoth Slayer]].
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] - Though only usable in his True Form, Doguemon can take multiple hits from the main threats in this stage and has enough damage to either kill peons outright, or get enemies within kill range for your other units.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - With his high damage and the Behemoth Slayer ability, he can efficiently chip Iguanidae Ibilujon as well as the peons in this stage. It goes without saying that he needs to be timed very well.

